# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
/test-results
/playwright-report
/blob-report
/.playwright
/playwright/.cache

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# Service worker build outputs, both written by scripts/build-service-worker.mjs. The
# precache manifest is generated from the build's content-hashed asset names, and sw.js is
# src/sw/service-worker.js with the build id stamped in. Edit the source, not these.
/public/precache.json
/public/sw.js

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local Claude Code configuration, not a project artifact
.claude/

# Local denylist terms. NEVER COMMIT — this file holds the identifying information the
# repo exists to keep out. The committed template is .denylist.local.example.
#
# The wildcard covers editor backups and hand-made copies (.bak, .save, ~, .orig).
# A copy of this file that .gitignore does not match is indistinguishable from the
# original in every way that matters, and is exactly how a local-only secret reaches
# a commit. The negation keeps the template committable.
.denylist.local*
!.denylist.local.example

# Private, non-public material: plan §7's writing samples and dictated notes, and any
# other pre-de-branding source read for reference and never committed. NEVER COMMIT —
# this material predates ADR-0001 and is expected to contain real manufacturer, product,
# and attendee names. The wildcard on the directory name covers hand-made copies for the
# same reason `.denylist.local*` does.
/private/
/private*

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files. `.env*` deliberately catches every variant, including ones nobody thinks
# to add (.env.production.local, .env.test). The negation keeps the value-free template
# committable — without it, .env.example is ignored like everything else and the
# onboarding file silently never lands.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
